WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.013
The layers shape the agent. A few features shape each session.

00:00:04.363 --> 00:00:08.523
Four worth knowing on day one: steer, undo, inspect, and run in parallel.

00:00:09.923 --> 00:00:14.531
Shift+Tab cycles the permission modes: auto, manual, accept edits, and plan.

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:17.072
Auto is the default in the terminal:

00:00:17.072 --> 00:00:20.236
a classifier blocks risky actions instead of asking.

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:22.606
Plan mode explores and writes a plan,

00:00:22.606 --> 00:00:25.663
without touching your source files until you approve it.

00:00:27.063 --> 00:00:29.247
Press Escape twice, or type /rewind,

00:00:29.247 --> 00:00:32.098
to restore the code, the conversation, or both.

00:00:32.448 --> 00:00:35.494
It won't undo files that only shell commands changed,

00:00:35.494 --> 00:00:37.333
and it's no replacement for git.

00:00:37.683 --> 00:00:42.398
Checkpoints are saved with the conversation, so rewind still works after you resume.

00:00:43.798 --> 00:00:47.190
/context shows what loaded, and what each part costs.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:51.359
It also suggests what to trim when a tool or a memory file gets heavy.

00:00:51.709 --> 00:00:55.911
/doctor runs a checkup of your installation, settings and rules files.

00:00:56.261 --> 00:00:58.181
Check both before you blame the model.

00:00:59.581 --> 00:01:03.313
Start with --worktree, and each session gets its own checkout,

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:05.299
so parallel work doesn't collide.

00:01:05.649 --> 00:01:09.935
Then subagents for side tasks, agent view to watch background sessions,

00:01:09.935 --> 00:01:13.798
and agent teams, still experimental, for agents that coordinate.

00:01:14.148 --> 00:01:15.688
Codex has the same ideas:

00:01:15.688 --> 00:01:21.231
/permissions for approvals and the sandbox, and /review for a second look at your changes.
